NAME
       ctype - classify and convert characters

SYNOPSIS
       #include <ctype.h>

       int isalpha(int c);   int isdigit(int c);   int isalnum(int c);
       int isspace(int c);   int isblank(int c);   int ispunct(int c);
       int isupper(int c);   int islower(int c);   int isxdigit(int c);
       int isprint(int c);   int isgraph(int c);   int iscntrl(int c);
       int tolower(int c);   int toupper(int c);

DESCRIPTION
       Classifies a single character and converts between cases. The
       argument is an unsigned char widened to int, or EOF; passing a
       plain signed char with the high bit set is undefined, so cast
       it: isalpha((unsigned char)*p).

       There is no locale, so these follow ASCII.

RETURN VALUE
       The is* functions return non-zero when the class matches.
       tolower and toupper return the converted character, or the
       argument unchanged when no conversion applies.

SEE ALSO
       string(3), strtol(3)
